{"tool_name":"multtest","contents":["bioconda","oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bioconductor-multtest","version":"2.66.0","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/html/multtest.html","license":"LGPL","summary":"Resampling-based multiple hypothesis testing","identifiers":["biotools:multtest","doi:10.1007/0-387-29362-0_15"],"description":"Non-parametric bootstrap and permutation resampling-based multiple testing procedures (including empirical Bayes methods) for controlling the family-wise error rate (FWER), generalized family-wise error rate (gFWER), tail probability of the proportion of false positives (TPPFP), and false discovery rate (FDR).  Several choices of bootstrap-based null distribution are implemented (centered, centered and scaled, quantile-transformed). Single-step and step-wise methods are available. Tests based on a variety of t- and F-statistics (including t-statistics based on regression parameters from linear and survival models as well as those based on correlation parameters) are included.  When probing hypotheses with t-statistics, users may also select a potentially faster null distribution which is multivariate normal with mean zero and variance covariance matrix derived from the vector influence function.  Results are reported in terms of adjusted p-values, confidence regions and test statistic cutoffs. The procedures are directly applicable to identifying differentially expressed genes in DNA microarray experiments.","license_file":"/lib/R/share/licenses/LGPL-3","build":{"number":0,"rpaths":["lib/R/lib/","lib/"],"run_exports":""},"requirements":{"build":[null,"make"],"host":["bioconductor-biobase >=2.70.0,<2.71.0","bioconductor-biocgenerics >=0.56.0,<0.57.0","r-base","r-mass","r-survival","libblas","liblapack","zlib","liblzma-devel"],"run":["bioconductor-biobase >=2.70.0,<2.71.0","bioconductor-biocgenerics >=0.56.0,<0.57.0","r-base","r-mass","r-survival"]},"source_url":["https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.